---
import ProjectShell from '../components/ProjectShell.astro';
import Fig from '../components/Fig.astro';
import Note from '../components/Note.astro';
---

<ProjectShell
    title="Swaplings"
    bg="#fff1df"
    ink="#2a1830"
    accent="#ff4f8b"
    class="swaplings"
>
    <section class="hero">
        <Fig folder="swaplings" src="swaplingsLogo.jpg" alt="Swaplings character collection and logo" ratio="4/3" eager sizes="(min-width: 1100px) 900px, 94vw" widths={[960, 1440, 1920]} radius="0" class="hero-logo" />
    </section>
    <p class="p-date p-date--solo">2025</p>

    <section class="p-wrap">
        <div class="p-intro">
            <p class="p-intro-lead">The portrayal of disabilities and diverse bodies in the toy and collectible market remains incredibly under represented. This project, Swaplings, is a series of stylised, 3D-printed action figures that explore inclusion and diversity through modular design and the representation of disabilities.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="p-wrap renders">
        <div class="renders-art">
            <Fig folder="swaplings" src="renders1.jpg" alt="Rendered Swaplings character collection" ratio="3/2" sizes="(min-width: 1440px) 1330px, 94vw" widths={[960, 1440, 1920]} radius="22px" />
        </div>
        <div class="side-notes">
            <Note>
                Detachable limbs of varying shapes, sizes, and colours can be mixed and matched to encourage playful interaction beyond conventional toy norms - modularity lets people experiment and be creative, allowing them to make their own versions of toys they own.
            </Note>
            <Note>
                Disabilities are part of the characters, but they are no more important than their shapes and personality, to ensure that representation is natural as opposed to tokenistic.
            </Note>
            <Note>
                Tangible agency is offered through this modularity, and the combination with bold design aims to make a product line that is both socially conscious and creatively engaging.
            </Note>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="p-wrap proto">
        <div class="proto-img">
            <Fig folder="swaplings" src="eg1.jpg" alt="Swaplings character study, example one" ratio="16/9" sizes="(min-width: 1440px) 1330px, 94vw" widths={[960, 1440, 1920]} radius="22px" />
        </div>
        <div class="proto-img">
            <Fig folder="swaplings" src="eg2.jpg" alt="Swaplings character study, example two" ratio="16/9" sizes="(min-width: 1440px) 1330px, 94vw" widths={[960, 1440, 1920]} radius="22px" />
        </div>
        <div class="proto-note">
            <Note>
                The 3D printed models were interactive prototypes that explored the modularity of the system. Additional accessories allow for absurd and creative play.
            </Note>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="p-wrap pack">
        <Fig folder="swaplings" src="box.jpg" alt="Swaplings packaging box" ratio="3840/1490" sizes="(min-width: 1440px) 1330px, 94vw" widths={[960, 1440, 1920]} radius="22px" />
        <div class="pack-row">
            <div class="p-cell p-cell--stretch" style="--cell:893/1391"><Fig folder="swaplings" src="panel.jpg" alt="Swaplings character information panel" fill sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 430px, 94vw" radius="22px" /></div>
            <div class="p-cell p-cell--stretch" style="--cell:4/3"><Fig folder="swaplings" src="logo.jpg" alt="Swaplings identity and logo artwork" fill sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 880px, 94vw" radius="22px" /></div>
        </div>
    </section>
</ProjectShell>

<style>
    .hero {
        display: grid;
        justify-items: center;
        padding: 1rem var(--pad) clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
        background: linear-gradient(180deg, #fff 0%, #fff calc(100% - clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem)), var(--bg) 100%);
    }

    .hero :global(.hero-logo) {
        width: min(100%, 58rem, calc(76svh * 4 / 3));
        background: #fff;
    }
    .renders,
    .proto {
        display: grid;
        gap: clamp(1rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
        padding-block: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    }
    .side-notes {
        display: grid;
        gap: 1.1rem 2rem;
    }
    .proto-note {
        max-width: 34rem;
    }

    .pack {
        display: grid;
        gap: var(--gap);
        padding-block: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem) clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    }

    .pack-row {
        display: grid;
        gap: var(--gap);
    }

    @media (min-width: 900px) {

        .side-notes {
            grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
        }

        .pack-row {
            grid-template-columns: 1fr 2.077fr;
        }
    }
</style>